# Running and verifying

> Both commit gates pass as of milestone 2, 2026-08-03. If one fails, you probably
> broke it — but read [docs/status.md](mdc:docs/status.md) before deciding, and never
> "fix" the game to satisfy an assertion you have not first shown to be right.

```sh
# Play.
Godot --path .

# Commit gate 1: plays a whole run badly on purpose and asserts the result.
Godot --headless --fixed-fps 60 --path . res://tools/smoke_run.tscn

# Commit gate 2: drives the states a successful run never reaches - downed, dead,
# revive, repair at each speed, rejected casts, and the failure path.
Godot --headless --fixed-fps 60 --path . res://tools/behaviour_checks.tscn

# Screenshots of 13 game states, into user://screenshots.
# Must run windowed - saving a viewport image needs a real rendering device.
Godot --fixed-fps 60 --resolution 1280x720 --path . res://tools/screenshot_run.tscn

# Regenerate route control points after changing the road shape.
python3 tools/road_calc.py --target 9000 --wavelength 2800
```

On this machine the binary is
`/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot`.

## What the smoke test asserts

Route length 9000 px, the four defenders starting in Follow inside their slot band,
the run completing, terrain events in order `Mud, Road, Mud, Road`, time on mud at
the ×0.60 factor, all six enemy groups firing, enemies both landing attacks and
dying, some defender reaching the Defend state, Arc Bolt being cast, the selection
and order counts being recorded, the squad staying inside the attack leash, and the
full telemetry key set. **Adding a telemetry field means updating
`tools/smoke_run.gd` too**, or the key-set assertion fails.

It asserts the duration band this build can actually produce, which is not yet the
three-minute floor of §7 — see [docs/status.md](mdc:docs/status.md) for why that is
correct rather than a bug.

## What behaviour_checks asserts

The paths a successful run never takes: an order reaching the selection and nobody
else, the 15-second downed timer ending in Dead with no collision shape, revive
working on a downed defender and refusing a dead one, cargo repair at Stop and not
at Fast, casts rejected for range, mana and being unimplemented, and cargo
destruction opening the result screen with `end_reason = cargo_destroyed`.

## Telemetry output

`user://telemetry`, which on macOS is
`~/Library/Application Support/Godot/app_userdata/MagicLogisticsInit`. One JSON per
run, named `run_<date>_P<profile>_seed<n>.json`, 35 keys.

## Standard of proof

An assertion is not a playtest. This project exists to evaluate **control feel**, so
"the smoke test passes" is not evidence that a control change is good. When a change
touches how the game feels, say so and ask for a play session rather than reporting
it as verified.

Report outcomes plainly: if the smoke test fails, paste the output. If you did not
run it, say you did not run it.
